prompt:
## Resumo
A sophisticated technical design system for modern operational platforms. It uses a clean 'instrumentation' aesthetic with light/dark modes, monospaced accents, halftone textures, and a structured grid system that feels both modern and utilitarian.

## Estilo Visual
{
  "summary": "A cold-light editorial B2B style: a fog-grey ground, cool slate ink and a single sky-blue accent, built on the contrast between a light quirky-geometric display face and small wide-tracked monospace labels. Photography is stripped to monochrome and run through a halftone dot screen, so the only colour on the page is the accent. Everything is square-cornered and shadowless — depth comes from tinted panels and hairlines, never elevation.",
  "style": {
    "description": "Maritime fog: cold morning light on granite. The palette is cool end to end — warm neutrals (cream, beige, tan) are strictly off-brand. The signature is a three-way type contrast: an airy light geometric display at 64px with heavy negative tracking, calm Inter body copy at 60% ink, and tiny uppercase monospace labels at 0.3–0.64px letter-spacing. Imagery never appears in colour; every photograph is grayscaled, contrast-boosted and overlaid with a fine halftone dot screen so it reads as a printed plate rather than a stock photo. One accent colour carries CTAs, the chart line and the eyebrow marks, and nothing else competes with it.",
    "prompt": "Create a cool-toned, square-cornered editorial B2B UI.\n- **Palette**: ground #F4F7FA (cool paper — never pure white, never cream), ink #14181D (cool slate near-black, never a warm black), body copy #14181D at 60%, tile icons #14181D at 50%, primary #4E9BE8, primary-deep #2F73C4 (used ONLY for small accent text under 14px, where the light blue fails contrast), surface #C3CFDB at 40%, secondary button #E6EDF4, hairline #D5DEE8, halftone plate base #F2F1E8.\n- **Typography**: display face 'Anybody' weight 300 (a light quirky geometric with a single-storey g and straight-tailed y; the licensed original is 'Parabole'). h1 64px/70.4px at -3.2px tracking; h2 40px/44px at -1.6px; oversized closing h2 64px/70.4px at -2.56px; FAQ question 20px/21.2px at -0.6px. Body in Inter 400: hero lead 18px/27px, section body 16px/24px. ALL labels, captions and button text in monospace (ui-monospace / Geist Mono) UPPERCASE: eyebrow and captions 10px/11px at 0.3px, testimonial role 12px/13.2px at 0.36px, feature tile label 16px/17.6px at 0.64px. Button labels use the display face at 12px/14.4px, 0.48px, uppercase.\n- **Hard rules**: border-radius 0 on every button, tile, panel and image band (the only exceptions are a 2px radius on testimonial cards and full-round monogram avatars). No drop shadows anywhere. No gradients on surfaces. Text contrast is non-negotiable — small uppercase accent labels take primary-deep, never primary.\n- **Imagery**: every photograph gets filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.3) brightness(0.92) plus a halftone dot screen overlay — two offset radial-gradient dot layers at 3px pitch in #F2F1E8, background-position 0 0 and 1.5px 1.5px, mix-blend-mode screen, opacity 0.42. Apply this identically to EVERY image on the page so they read as one set."
  },
  "layout_and_structure": {
    "description": "A single centred 1064px column inside a 1440px frame, with 40px outer gutters and 20px inner padding. Sections are separated by 96px of top padding with a 40px internal gap. The page alternates between quiet light text blocks and full-width dark monochrome image bands, and the first headline sits at exactly 200px from the top of the page.",
    "prompts": [
      {
        "part": "Navigation",
        "prompt": "Sticky header on the ground colour, 12px vertical padding, content constrained to 1064px with 20px inner padding. Left: logo lockup — a 24px inline-SVG triangular three-node graph (two nodes in ink, the lower-right node in #4E9BE8, joined by 1.4px round-capped lines) plus a 20px display-face wordmark. Centre: nav links in the display face, 12px uppercase at 0.48px tracking. Right: a ghost text link plus a #4E9BE8 primary button. Below 768px the centre nav collapses to a hamburger."
      },
      {
        "part": "Hero",
        "prompt": "The h1 must sit exactly 200px from the top of the page — subtract the header's height from the hero's top padding to achieve this, do not simply stack 200px under the header. h1 at 64px, then an 18px lead capped at 770px so it never runs past two lines, then two buttons side by side: primary #4E9BE8 and secondary #E6EDF4, both 16px/20px padding with a 16px ↗ arrow glyph. Buttons go full-width and stack under 640px."
      },
      {
        "part": "Measuring-ruler rule",
        "prompt": "A full-width instrument rule sitting directly above the hero image band, overlapping its top edge. A row of ~60 thin 14px tick marks in ink at 18% opacity, with the FIRST tick doubled in weight, 26px tall and coloured #4E9BE8. Above the ticks, two 10px uppercase monospace labels at 20% opacity pushed to the far left and far right (e.g. ARTIFICIAL … INTELLIGENCE). A 1px #D5DEE8 hairline closes the bottom."
      },
      {
        "part": "Monochrome image band",
        "prompt": "A full-column band 600px tall on a #F2F1E8 base, holding one cover-fitted photograph with the halftone treatment applied. Used for the hero and repeated as a short 220px band above the footer. No caption, no overlay text — the band is a plate, not a hero card."
      },
      {
        "part": "Section head",
        "prompt": "Eyebrow, then heading, then body, with 20px between each. Eyebrow: a 6px solid #4E9BE8 square followed by a 10px uppercase monospace label in #2F73C4. Heading: display face 40px, deliberately hard-broken over two lines. Body: Inter 16px/24px at 60% ink, capped at 720px so it never reaches four lines."
      },
      {
        "part": "Feature grid",
        "prompt": "Three across, 16px gaps. Each tile is 150px tall with 20px padding on #C3CFDB at 40%, laid out as a column with space-between: a 32px thin-stroke line icon (1.5px, 50% ink) at the top-left and a monospace uppercase label at the bottom-left. Critically, the 'NO. 1' … 'NO. 6' caption sits OUTSIDE and BELOW each tile in 10px monospace, not inside it. Two across between 640 and 1024px, one across below 640px."
      },
      {
        "part": "Testimonials",
        "prompt": "Two cards, 16px gap, each minimum 287px with 20px padding on #C3CFDB at 40% and a 2px radius, arranged as a column with space-between. Top: a small customer lockup — an 18px thin line mark plus a 15px Inter medium wordmark, both in #5B6672. Middle: the quote in Inter 16px/24px at full ink. Bottom: a 48px round monogram avatar (#CBD8E6 fill, #3C4A5A initials) beside a display-face name and a 12px uppercase monospace role. Use monogram initials — never photographs of people."
      },
      {
        "part": "FAQ",
        "prompt": "Two columns: a stacked display-face heading on the left (about 280px wide) and the question list on the right. Each row is 20px vertical padding, question left in the display face at 20px, and a 14px × 1px ink dash on the right as the toggle affordance, separated by 1px #D5DEE8 hairlines with a hairline above the first row. Stacks to one column below 768px."
      },
      {
        "part": "Closing CTA",
        "prompt": "An oversized 64px display heading with the body copy beneath it on the left, and the same two buttons pinned right, aligned to the top. Below it, the short 220px monochrome image band, then the footer. Stacks vertically below 768px with full-width buttons."
      },
      {
        "part": "Footer",
        "prompt": "A 20px-padded row: logo lockup left, monospace uppercase nav centred, X and LinkedIn glyphs right. Then a 1px #D5DEE8 hairline, and a legal row with the copyright in 10px display face at 60% ink on the left and Status / Terms / Privacy on the right."
      }
    ]
  },
  "special_ui_components": [
    {
      "component": "Halftone Plate",
      "description": "The technique that makes every photograph on the page look like one printed set rather than assorted stock imagery.",
      "prompt": "Wrap the image in a position:relative container with background #F2F1E8 and overflow hidden. The img is object-fit:cover with filter: grayscale(1) contrast(1.3) brightness(0.92). Add an ::after overlay at inset 0 with pointer-events:none carrying TWO stacked radial-gradient dot layers — radial-gradient(circle at 50% 50%, #F2F1E8 0.85px, transparent 1.15px) repeated at background-size 3px 3px with background-position 0 0 and 1.5px 1.5px to fake a hex grid — set to mix-blend-mode:screen at opacity 0.42. Increase the pitch to 4–5px for a coarser, more obviously printed dot."
    },
    {
      "component": "Dark Glass Metric Panel",
      "description": "The page's one moment of depth and its only use of colour besides the CTAs — a translucent dark panel floating on a monochrome image band.",
      "prompt": "Centre a 680px panel on the image band: background rgba(13,17,23,0.66), 1px rgba(255,255,255,0.14) border, backdrop-filter blur(6px), 24px/28px/20px padding, square corners, z-index above the halftone overlay. Header row: a 15px Inter medium title in #E8EEF5 with an 11px uppercase monospace sub-label at 55% beneath it, and right-aligned legend chips each pairing an 18px × 2px colour bar with an 11px monospace label. Below, an inline-SVG line chart on a 624×216 viewBox: three horizontal gridlines at 8/18/8 percent white, a rising #4E9BE8 series at 2.2px with round caps and a 12% opacity area fill beneath it, a flat dashed grey comparison series at 1.6px with a 5/4 dash array, and an endpoint dot with a soft halo (r=7 at 20% plus r=3.4 solid). Axis labels in 10px monospace at 45% white. Below 640px the header stacks and the legend wraps under the title."
    },
    {
      "component": "Eyebrow Mark",
      "description": "The small repeating device that opens every section.",
      "prompt": "A flex row with 8px gap: a 6px × 6px solid #4E9BE8 square that never scales, followed by a 10px/11px uppercase monospace label at 0.3px tracking in #2F73C4. Never use the lighter #4E9BE8 for this label — at 10px it drops below readable contrast on the #F4F7FA ground."
    },
    {
      "component": "Arrow Button",
      "description": "The only interactive element on the page; square, flat and label-led.",
      "prompt": "Inline-flex with 12px gap and 16px/20px padding, zero radius, no border, no shadow. Primary is #4E9BE8, secondary is #E6EDF4 — both keep #14181D ink text rather than white, because the blue is light enough that dark text is the higher-contrast choice. Label in the display face at 12px uppercase, 0.48px tracking, followed by a 16px ↗ glyph drawn as a 1px stroked inline SVG. Minimum 44px tall and full-width below 640px."
    }
  ]
}


